<Data>Data Flow Analysis : LTE-A_20MHz_5CCs Analysis&#x000D;&#x000A;9/26/2014..4:28 PM&#x000D;&#x000A;LTE_A_DL_Src_RangeCheck &apos;LTE-A_20MHz_5CCs__LTE_A_DL_Src_1.LTE_DL_MIMO_4Ant_Src_RangeCheck&apos;: &#x000D;&#x000A; &#x000D;&#x000A;System Configurations:&#x000D;&#x000A;1. Frame structure is TDD; Uplink-donwlink configuration is 0: {D,S,U,U,U,D,S,U,U,U}.&#x000D;&#x000A;2. For special subframes in TDD, the configuration is 0. The lengths in units of OFDM symbols for DwPTS/GP/UpPTS are 3/10/1.&#x000D;&#x000A;3. Channel bandwidth is 20 MHz.&#x000D;&#x000A;4. Cell ID is 0.&#x000D;&#x000A;5. Normal cyclic prefix is employed.&#x000D;&#x000A;6. The transmission mode of each UE is {Mode 4, Mode 4, Mode 4, Mode 4, Mode 4, Mode 4}.&#x000D;&#x000A;7. The number of Tx antennas is .2.&#x000D;&#x000A;8. The number of CRS (Cell specific Reference Signal) ports is 2.&#x000D;&#x000A;9. The mapping type of virtual resource blocks to physical resource blocks for all radio frames is Localized.&#x000D;&#x000A;10. Number of OFDM symbols used for transmission of PDCCHs of the 10 subframes are {0,0,N/A,N/A,N/A,0,0,N/A,N/A,N/A}.&#x000D;&#x000A;11. PDCCH Formats of the 10 downlink subframes are: &#x000D;&#x000A;  For each subframe, the first 6 elements indicate the formats of the PDCCH candidates in UE specific search space, while the rest 4 elements indicate the formats of PDCCH candicates in common search space.&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 0:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 1:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 2:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 3:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 4:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 5:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 6:    0  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A  N/A&#x000D;&#x000A;  Subframe 7:   